cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this brief, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "What Makes an AI Character Worth Coming Back To? Humor, Personality, Emotional Connection, and the Art of Meaningful AI Roleplay"
abstract: >-
  A research-informed design brief, written by the founder of a commercial AI
  character product, arguing that compelling AI characters are defined by the
  quality and consistency of the character experience rather than by how
  explicit they can be. It uses four official ChatBrat scenarios to illustrate
  distinct dimensions (personality and voice, humor, emotional responsiveness,
  chemistry and pacing, creative initiative, memory and user agency) and
  proposes a checklist for evaluating them. It is not an independent study and
  makes no product-performance claims.
